Title: Enable Jenkins Resource Root URL on jenkins-biss-cicd

Summary:
The BISS Playwright pipeline publishes an HTML test report with the HTML Publisher plugin
("Test Dashboard" link on each build). Jenkins' default content security policy strips the
report's styling and scripts, so it shows as plain text. Jenkins' recommended fix is the
Resource Root URL, which serves report files from a separate hostname instead of relaxing
the security policy.

Requested:
1. A second OpenShift Route to the existing Jenkins service in namespace biss-cicd, e.g.
   jenkins-biss-cicd-resources.apps.services1.agriculture.gov.ie (TLS edge, same certificate
   as the main route).
2. Manage Jenkins > System > "Serve resource files from another domain":
   Resource Root URL = https://jenkins-biss-cicd-resources.apps.services1.agriculture.gov.ie/
   (or the equivalent setting in the Jenkins configuration-as-code).

Not requested: disabling or relaxing the Jenkins content security policy.

Impact: no change to logins or permissions. HTML reports of all jobs on this Jenkins display
correctly. Links to report files become short-lived and per user.

Reference: https://www.jenkins.io/doc/book/security/user-content/#resource-root-url
